# Internal Flash Procedure: {{ device.vendor }} {{ device.model }}

**Device ID:** `{{ device.id }}`
**Tier:** {{ device.status.tier }} | **Score:** {{ device.status.score }}/100

## 1. Prerequisites

- External programmer backup already stored and verified (see `recover.md`).
- **NEVER** overwrite the IFD, ME, or GbE regions internally. Preserve the GbE region so the Ethernet MAC address stays intact.
- Confirm 3.3 V / 1.8 V external programmer availability before flashing in case recovery is needed.

## 2. Mandatory 3-Read Internal BIOS Backup

Run on the target host OS (not inside a container):

```bash
sudo flashrom -p internal --ifd -i bios -r bios_read1.bin
sudo flashrom -p internal --ifd -i bios -r bios_read2.bin
sudo flashrom -p internal --ifd -i bios -r bios_read3.bin
sha256sum bios_read1.bin bios_read2.bin bios_read3.bin
```

All three SHA-256 digests MUST match.

## 3. Flash Only the BIOS Region

```bash
cb4a verify --id {{ device.id }} --rom out/builds/{{ device.id }}/coreboot.rom
sudo flashrom -p internal --ifd -i bios -w out/builds/{{ device.id }}/coreboot.rom
```

Shut down completely (`sudo poweroff`), wait 10 seconds, and power on.
